{{Quote|Stick around for a while, why don't ya?|Stinkfly after shooting slime from his eyes.<ref name="OPaPP1">''[[Of Predators and Prey: Part 1]]''</ref>}}
Stinkfly's primary ability is to squirt high-pressured streams of green, slimy liquid from the glands located inside of his eyestalks and mouth. Special filters in his underbelly absorb particles of matter from the air to create the slime.{{Refn|[[:File:Stinkfly Alien Creation Card.png]]|group = Bandai|name = card}} This slime is strong enough to hold a helicopter<ref name="TL">''[[Tough Luck]]''</ref> and hold down [[Crabdozer (Transformation)|Crabdozer]].<ref name="OPaPP1"/> Stinkfly is capable of utilizing his slime in a number of useful capacities, such as ensnaring his opponents,<ref name="DAA" /> or blasting a stream of it out of his mouth, solid enough to pull himself upwards like a makeshift grappling hook.<ref name="The Krakken">''[[The Krakken]]''</ref>

Stinkfly can produce slime of differing properties, and he can instinctively choose which type of slime to expel.{{Refn|[[:File:Stinkfly Slime Type.png]]|group = MW}} Examples include an immobilizing adhesive<ref name="TT">''[[Tourist Trap]]''</ref><ref name="TL"/><ref>''[[A Change of Face]]''</ref> and a flammable toxin.<ref name="Grudge Match">''[[Grudge Match]]''</ref>

Stinkfly possesses two dragon-shaped insectoid wings that allow quick and agile flying and can change directions at exceptional paces.He can fly at over 60 mph, but only for short distances.{{Refn|group = Bandai|name = card}}

Stinkfly's black tail is extremely sharp with a stinger-like end that can tear and rend through steel almost effortlessly.<ref name="TT"/> His tail is an ultra sensitive receptor, making it like an antenna.{{Refn|[[:File:The Return Pop-up (6).png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref>''[[The Return]]''</ref> Stinkfly's claws and sharp-pointed legs allow him to cling onto solid surfaces.<ref name="BwaV"/>

Stinkfly has great strength in proportion to his body, being able to carry heavy loads while maintaining steady flight.<ref name="MC"/> His carrying power comes to its limit when holding something very heavy, shown when he could keep flying while [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]] was holding onto him.<ref name="Secrets" /> Stinkfly is also strong and dense enough to knock back a [[Tetramand (Classic)|Tetramand]] if he flies into them at full speed.<ref name="Framed">''[[Framed]]''</ref>

Stinkfly's exoskeletal body is fairly strong, allowing him to survive unscathed while being smashed through buildings and being caught inside a large explosion.<ref name="Secrets">''[[Secrets]]''</ref> His tough exoskeleton is bulletproof.{{Refn|group = Bandai|name = card}}

Stinkfly has enhanced hearing, as he was able to hear a conversation over the sound of a helicopter while both he and it were flying.<ref name="B10VSN10P1">''[[Ben 10 vs. Negative 10: Part 1]]''</ref>

The flexible nature of Stinkfly's eyestalks give him 360-degree vision, as he is able to move two eyes at the back of his head and keep the other two eyes at the front of his head.<ref name="K11" />

Stinkfly is accompanied by a natural odor-like stink that comes from the oils he secretes to keep his exoskeleton joints moving.{{Refn|[[:File:Stinkfly's Stink.png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="K11"/>

Stinkfly is capable of releasing both toxic gas and methane gas,{{Refn|[[:File:Classic Stinkfly Can Shoot Gas.png]]|group = DR}} the former of which was demonstrated when he was a 4-year-old to kill plant-like creatures.<ref>''[[Don't Drink the Water]]''</ref>

===Non-Canon Powers and Abilities===
====Cartoon Network Action Pack!====
Stinkfly can generate powerful gusts of wind with his wings, capable of holding up an airplane.{{Refn|''[[Sonic Boom]]''|group = AP}}

====[[Battle With Way Big]]====
Stinkfly can perform an attack that involves green energy surrounding his body, which can be used as a charge.

==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
Secrets (806).png|Vulnerable Wings
Krakken (1297).png|Wet Wings
Lurk (870).png|Unable to Swim
DAA (519).png|Detected by Smell
DepreyPresa1P56.png|Buglizard Predation
DepreyPresa2P128.png|Electricity Vulnerability
</gallery>
An opponent could take advantage of Stinkfly's wings, as if they are held down, Stinkfly is unable to fly.<ref name="Secrets" /><ref name="DWS">''[[Divided We Stand]]''</ref> If his wings get completely soaked in water, they become limp and heavy and he'll be completely incapable of flight until they dry off.<ref name="The Krakken" /><ref name="TLB">''[[They Lurk Below]]''</ref>

Stinkfly is unable to swim due to his unbalanced body weight and thin limbs.<ref name="TLB" />

A more minor inconvenience is Stinkfly's odor, which can be a problem if he is trying to hide from anything or anyone that can smell.<ref name="DAA" />

Being a Lepidopterran, Stinkfly is at a massive disadvantage against a [[Buglizard]] due to its slime neutralizing fog.<ref name="OPaPP1" /><ref name="OPaPP2">''[[Of Predators and Prey: Part 2]]''</ref>

Stinkfly is vulnerable against electricity, as shown when he was shocked while trying to attack [[Phil Billings (Classic)|Phil]] as [[Terroranchula]].<ref name="OPaPP2" />

Stinkfly is implied to be vulnerable to fire, as shown when he backed away from a growing fire.<ref name="TT"/>

==History==
===Ben 10===
*Stinkfly first appeared in ''[[Washington B.C.]]'', where he saved [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] from the [[Mutant Parrot]] and defeated [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]].
*In ''[[The Krakken]]'', Stinkfly battled [[Jonah Melville]] and his crew until the former escaped with an unconscious [[Mr. Shaw]].
*In ''[[Kevin 11 (Episode)|Kevin 11]]'', Stinkfly escaped the police with [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]].
*In ''[[Tourist Trap]]'', Stinkfly scared a kid in a car and saved a truck driver from a fire.
*In ''[[Secrets]]'', Stinkfly defeated two [[Mechadroid|Mechadroids]], but was defeated and reverted by [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]]. 
**Also, Stinkfly appeared as one of the many alien templates used for Vilgax's army in an imaginary sequence.
*In ''[[The Big Tick]]'', Stinkfly freed [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]] and Gwen from some tentacles and fought the [[Leader Alien]], [[Interpreter Alien]] and [[Enforcer Alien]].
*In ''[[Framed]]'', Kevin used Stinkfly four times to escape from police and from Ben.
*In ''[[Ultimate Weapon]]'', Stinkfly flew Gwen and Max to the temple of Ek Chuaj, but the Omnitrix timed out before he could reach the temple.
*In ''[[Camp Fear]]'', Stinkfly flew over [[Camp Opinicon]] while Gwen dropped athlete's foot powder all over the spores that were created by the [[Mycelium]] in order to destroy them.
*In ''[[Tough Luck]]'', Stinkfly stopped a helicopter from crashing while Lucky Girl saved a man who fell off of it.
*In ''[[They Lurk Below]]'', Stinkfly saved Gwen and [[Eddie Grand Smith|Eddie]] from drowning and escaped some [[Cyber Squid]]s. After he fell in the water and couldn't fly, they made their way through some vents and found some speedboats.
*In ''[[Back With a Vengeance]]'', Stinkfly appeared five times. Firstly, Stinkfly flew a man back to his boat. Secondly, he made money doing tourist jobs and spat slime into Gwen's pudding as a prank. Later, he escaped [[Kevin 11]] before turning into [[Four Arms (Classic)|Four Arms]]. Then, he was briefly seen with Max and Gwen before reverting. Lastly, in the [[Null Void (Classic)|Null Void]], Stinkfly escaped from Vilgax before running into Gwen and was forced to surrender after Kevin grabbed her.
*In ''[[Ben 10,000 (Episode)|Ben 10,000]]'', Stinkfly tried to help [[Ben 10,000 (Original)|Future]] [[Four Arms (Classic)|Four Arms]] fight [[Dr. Animo (Original Future)|Future Dr. Animo]], but was restrained by the former.
*In ''[[A Change of Face]]'', Stinkfly stopped a fire caused by [[Charmcaster (Classic)|Charmcaster]] and was caught in her [[Spells (Classic)|spell]] before being knocked out of it by Gwen.
*In ''[[Merry Christmas]]'', Stinkfly acted as a reindeer to pull Santa's sleigh.
*In ''[[Super Alien Hero Buddy Adventures (Episode)|Super Alien Hero Buddy Adventures]]'', Stinkfly and Gwen spied on [[Abel North]].
*In ''[[The Return]]'', Stinkfly caught some escaped prisoners with Gwen and Max's help.
*In '''''[[Ben 10: Secret of the Omnitrix]]''''', Stinkfly tried to chase after Dr. Animo but was switched into [[Wildmutt]] due to an Omnitrix glitch.
*In ''[[Don't Drink the Water]]'', 4-year-old Stinkfly (Stinkyfly) defeated [[Hex (Classic)|Hex]]'s mutated plants.
*In ''[[Ben 10 vs. Negative 10: Part 1]]'', Stinkfly caught some criminals.
*In '''''[[Ben 10: Destroy All Aliens]]''''', Stinkfly appeared thrice. Firstly, Stinkfly attacked Ben in a dream. Later, Stinkfly battled the [[Way Big (Classic)|Evil Way Big]] only to change back after a short time. Finally, Stinkfly was defeated by [[Azmuth's Father|Retaliator]] before the Omnitrix switched him into [[Heatblast (Classic)|Heatblast]].
*In ''[[The Forge of Creation]]'', Stinkfly was defeated by [[Ultimate Aggregor]].

===Five Years Prior to Omniverse=== 
*In ''[[A Jolt From the Past]]'', Stinkfly was defeated by a [[Nosedeenian (Classic)|Nosedeenian]].
*In ''[[Of Predators and Prey: Part 2]]'', Stinkfly teased [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] and battled [[Phil Billings (Classic)|Phil]] as [[Terroranchula]].

===Alien Force=== 
*Stinkfly was locked by the Omnitrix's reconfiguration in ''[[Ben 10 Returns: Part 1]]''.

===Ultimate Alien===
*In ''[[Ben 10,000 Returns]]'', Stinkfly was re-unlocked by [[Ben 10,000 (Ultimate Alien)|Ben 10,000]].
*In ''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Ben 10/Generator Rex: Heroes United]]'', Stinkfly appeared as one of the many aliens when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was explaining his story to [[Rex Salazar (Generator Rex)|Rex]].

===Omniverse===
*In ''[[Of Predators and Prey: Part 1]]'', Stinkfly defeated [[Crabdozer (Transformation)|Crabdozer]], but was defeated by [[Buglizard (Transformation)|Buglizard]].
*In ''[[Of Predators and Prey: Part 2]]'', Stinkfly escaped from [[Slamworm]] and was trapped by Buglizard.
*In ''[[Malefactor]]'', Stinkfly was dunked in the Ben 10: Dunk Tank.
*In ''[[Malgax Attacks]]'', [[Skurd]] used Stinkfly's wings while [[Blukic]] and [[Driba]] tried to remove him from the [[Omnitrix (Omniverse)|Omnitrix]].
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Stinkfly appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

===[[Original Future Timeline|Original Future]]===
*In ''[[Ben 10,000 (Episode)|Ben 10,000]]'', Stinkfly was defeated by [[Vilgax (Original Future)|Vilgax]], so he switched into [[XLR8 (Classic)|XLR8]].

